column86:
The error style I&#x27;ve always liked best is that of Objective-C.<p><pre><code>  NSError* error = nil;
  [object doSomething: foo error: &error];
  if(error){

  }
</code></pre>
I find exceptions to be rather overkill for most error type problems to begin and with the ObjC system it&#x27;s easy to ignore errors that may not be critical.<p><pre><code>  [object doSomething: foo error: nil];</code></pre>
